sn47.38:4.2 starts: As he dwells thus contemplating phenomena in phenomena,
an4.2:1.1 starts: At Sāvatthī. “Bhikkhus, one who does not possess four things
an4.2:1.3 starts: (1) One who does not possess noble virtuous behavior
an4.2:1.4 starts: (2) One who does not possess noble concentration …
an4.2:1.5 starts: (3) One who does not possess noble wisdom …
an4.2:1.6 starts: (4) One who does not possess noble liberation is said
an4.2:1.7 starts: One who does not possess these four things is said
an4.2:2.1 starts: “But, bhikkhus, one who possesses four things is said
an4.2:2.3 starts: (1) One who possesses noble virtuous behavior is said
an4.2:2.4 starts: (2) One who possesses noble concentration …
an4.2:2.5 starts: (3) One who possesses noble wisdom …
an4.2:2.6 starts: (4) One who possesses noble liberation is said
an4.2:2.7 starts: One who possesses these four things is said
